{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport ast, hashlib, json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nroot=Path('/workspace')\nprotocol='1a10f150c0b3977043072cd01f67a339c5c476f15c7847d04fa3acf9ce71e216'\nparent='g2-r0004-context_only'\nspecs=[('source_replay','source_control.py','control'),('embedding_half','candidate.py','candidate'),('dense_half','dense_half.py','control'),('both_half','compact_both.py','candidate')]\nvariants=[]\nfor name,file,role in specs:\n    tree=ast.parse((root/file).read_text())\n    config=next(ast.literal_eval(n.value) for n in tree.body if isinstance(n,ast.Assign) and any(isinstance(t,ast.Name) and t.id=='CONFIG' for t in n.targets))\n    note={\n      'source_replay':'Exact unchanged source and original CONFIG. Same-seed replay checks reproducibility and contemporaneous cost, not independent repetition.',\n      'embedding_half':'Reduce embedding width 16 to 8; preserve scorer/tower hidden widths. Input/output widths derived from embeddings shrink. All information, compression and gradient routing retained.',\n      'dense_half':'Keep embeddings at 16; halve scorer widths 64/32 to 32/16 and tower widths 128/64 to 64/32. Dense-only factorial control; not expected to materially reduce total parameter storage.',\n      'both_half':'Combine embedding width 8 with half-width scorer/towers; compare against both single-factor cells to detect interaction.'\n    }[name]\n    variants.append(dict(name=name,file=file,role=role,config=config,note=note+' Source SHA256='+hashlib.sha256((root/file).read_bytes()).hexdigest()+'. No numerical execution in preparation.'))\nfixed=[\n    'Protocol '+protocol+'; frozen released data identities, train/validation boundaries, all four labels and official_offline history visibility.',\n    'One scratch-training pass, host seed 20262027, batch 8192, history length 100, loading, BF16/TF32 policy and all host optimizer settings.',\n    'Ten fixed temporal blocks; thirty uniform/feedback-stratified means; count compensation and all thirty slots scored in each scorer call.',\n    'Unnormalized action-aware local activation; separate four-task towers; sum of four BCEs; auxiliary scorer and item/action gradients blocked, auxiliary context gradients allowed.',\n    'Same feature identities, vocabulary sizes, padding and embedding-sharing relations; no new inputs, labels, derived statistics, loss hook or protocol edits.'\n]\nconfounds=[\n    'Width changes alter random-number consumption and initial functions, even at the same seed; they are paired training recipes, not identical initial weights.',\n    'Embedding width also changes downstream input widths and representation/interaction rank. This study estimates their joint effect and cannot isolate table storage from rank.',\n    'Joint scorer/tower shrinking does not identify scorer versus tower redundancy separately.',\n    'Fixed one-pass optimization can favor one width through conditioning or regularization. Results apply to the frozen recipe, not converged optima.',\n    'Latency depends on bandwidth, kernel utilization, loading and device conditions; parameter savings alone do not establish measured speedup.'\n]\ncontrasts=[]\ndef contrast(intervention,control,support,negative,extra=None):\n    return dict(parent_ref=parent,intervention=intervention,control=control,held_fixed=fixed,remaining_confounds=confounds+(extra or []),decision_if_supported=support,decision_if_not_supported=negative)\ncontrasts.append(contrast('embedding_half minus source_replay, and both_half minus dense_half: embedding width 16 -> 8 at each fixed dense level.','source_replay and dense_half; also contextualize against existing '+parent+' and baseline-din without treating them as capacity-matched controls.','If click retention and the declared parameter/cost targets hold, repeat the better embedding-reduced cell with its unchanged source under host-authorized paired seeds.','If both embedding contrasts consistently lose more than the retention margin, reject width 8 within this recipe; consider a prospectively declared width 12 or source-specific allocation later. A single failed run is not mechanism refutation.'))\ncontrasts.append(contrast('dense_half minus source_replay, and both_half minus embedding_half: halve scorer and task-tower hidden widths at each embedding level.','source_replay and embedding_half.','If dense shrinking preserves quality and lowers measured latency, retain it; if retaining full dense capacity rescues width-8 quality, prioritize embedding_half as an allocation with more dense capacity at almost the same total storage.','If dense shrinkage harms quality without useful cost reduction, retain source dense widths; do not infer embeddings are necessary from a dense-only failure.'))\ncontrasts.append(contrast('Compute the AUC interaction (both_half - embedding_half) - (dense_half - source_replay), plus corresponding latency/cost contrasts.','All four cells constitute the 2x2 factorial, including the unchanged source.','If a combined reduction works only with one dense level, report the interaction and reserve a component/replacement control before attributing the result to either factor alone.','If interaction is small relative to uncertainty, describe additive effects provisionally; absence of detectable interaction in one seed does not establish independence.'))\ncontrasts.append(contrast('Same-seed source_replay versus the archived '+parent+' at exact original source/config hashes.','Existing '+parent+'; baseline-din is the shared descriptive reference.','If metrics reproduce within numerical tolerance and timing is stable, use the contemporary replay as the factorial anchor. It is not an independent random initialization.','If replay click AUC differs by more than 0.0001 or the source/config/feature-map identities differ, stop interpretation, preserve the receipt and diagnose provenance or execution before additional comparisons.'))\nstudy=dict(\n id='g1-t001-capacity-2x2-e8-densehalf',protocol_ref=protocol,\n evidence_refs=['baseline-din',parent,'paper:din','framework:unirank/pytorch/layers/embeddings/feature_embedding.py','framework:unirank/pytorch/layers/activations.py'],\n question='Can the stronger source preserve full-validation click AUC while reducing parameters and measured inference cost by shrinking embedding and/or dense capacity under the frozen one-pass recipe?',\n hypothesis='Observed: '+parent+' has click AUC 0.660646940486458 versus baseline-din 0.6555440824200336, but 31,793,216 of 32,060,453 parameters (99.17%) are embeddings. Its model-only batch p50/p95 are 11.726/11.864 ms; these observations do not prove redundant capacity. Mechanism hypothesis: target-aware compressed pooling may need less embedding rank and dense nonlinear width than currently allocated, allowing useful predictive information to survive lower-dimensional representations. A 2x2 width reduction tests whether storage-dominant embeddings and compute-relevant dense layers can shrink independently or jointly. This is an efficiency/capacity study of the existing source, not a new architecture or priority claim.',\n nearest_work=[\n    dict(source_ref='trial://'+parent,verification='implementation_checked',difference='Exact closest architectural control: preserve its uniform/feedback summaries, action-aware DIN scorer, context-only auxiliary embedding updates and separate task heads. Change only embedding and hidden widths, plus a private architecture copy to enforce requested embedding dimensions.'),\n    dict(source_ref='paper:din',verification='read',difference='Archived v4 primary text inspected at lines 219-334 (content SHA256 5fee25f33f375e51b3ee9417d376ff9dbe2ea3628c932a7679ddfeb0feaaade2). Inherit target-conditioned local activation, unnormalized weighted pooling and Dice. The local source adds compression, multi-feedback routing and gradient gates; this proposal studies widths within th